# steward/node — household hub runtime

What belongs here: the crate's modules under `src/`, its integration tests, the multi-node
simulation harness under `simulation/`, the Nix packaging, and `seam-registry.yaml`, which
registers each decision surface. Hub composition (which hub owns which method) routes to the
`elohim-hub-boundaries-design` epic, and reach vocabulary routes to
`reach-vocabulary-frontend-strand.md`. Neither is decided in this crate (`CLAUDE.md`, "Concern
routing").

`covers: subtree` is the ownership claim. The one edit-time signal lives in `src/.epr-meta`: a
new decision surface must answer the concern canon and be registered before it ships. The
hub-optional floor is the design rail every change here serves: a device with no hub is still a
full participant, and this node only enhances what a lone device already does.
